  - question: Does PCOS mean I have cysts on my ovaries?
    answer: >-
      Not exactly. The "cysts" are small, fluid-filled sacs where eggs
      develop. Many people with PCOS have them, but you can have PCOS without
      them, and you can have them without PCOS.
  - question: Can I get pregnant if I have PCOS?
    answer: >-
      Yes. Many people with PCOS get pregnant, sometimes with help from
      fertility treatment. PCOS is a common, treatable cause of fertility
      problems.
